FatFs in the PC/GEOS tree
=========================

This directory contains FatFs, the generic FAT file system module by ChaN
(http://elm-chan.org/fsw/ff/), release R0.16 with patch 2. It is licensed
under the FatFs license, a 1-clause BSD style license (see LICENSE.txt).

It is built as the host library "fatfs" (Installed/Tools/fatfs) and is used
by host tools that create or modify FAT disk images, currently img86box.

Files
-----
  ff.c, ff.h, diskio.h       FatFs, unmodified from upstream
  ffconf.h                   FatFs configuration for the PC/GEOS tools
  00readme.txt, 00history.txt, LICENSE.txt
                             upstream documentation and license
  fatimg.c, fatimg.h         PC/GEOS glue: FatFs media access interface
                             (disk_read/disk_write/...) on top of host
                             image files, one region per FatFs drive

Configuration (ffconf.h) differs from upstream defaults in:
  FF_USE_MKFS = 1      create file systems (f_mkfs)
  FF_USE_CHMOD = 1     set attributes and time stamps (f_chmod, f_utime)
  FF_USE_LABEL = 1     volume label
  FF_CODE_PAGE = 437   DOS default code page for 8.3 names
  FF_VOLUMES = 2       target image and FreeDOS template image

Long file names are disabled on purpose (FF_USE_LFN = 0): the images are
used by DOS and PC/GEOS, which only see 8.3 names.

Updating
--------
Replace ff.c, ff.h and diskio.h with a newer release, then merge the
settings above into the new ffconf.h (keep the FFCONF_DEF revision of the
new release).
